module dbcoConjugationQC
module plasmidLigationQC
module viabilityDetection
module proxseqLibraryQC
module plaProductDetection

manifest PBS
manifest DMSO
manifest DBCO_NHS_Ester
manifest AzideDNA_OligoA
manifest AzideDNA_OligoB
manifest BlockerBSA_PBS
manifest LigationBuffer
manifest T4_Ligase
manifest SingleCells
manifest TruStain_FcX
manifest PropidiumIodide
manifest DeadCellRemovalKit
manifest SalmonSpermDNA
manifest RNaseInhibitor
manifest AMPureXP_Beads
manifest SPRIselect_Beads
manifest KAPA_HiFi_ReadyMix
manifest BufferEB
manifest NucleaseFreeWater
manifest Chromium_GELBeads
manifest Chromium_Oil
manifest dNTP_Mix
manifest PhiX_Control
manifest NextSeq_MidOutput_Kit

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Proximity Sequencing (Prox-seq) for the detection of mRNA,
// extracellular proteins and extracellular protein complexes
// in single cells.
// Vistain, Keisham, Xia, Phan & Tay - Nature Protocols
// Volume 19, December 2024, pp. 3568-3589
// DOI: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41596-024-01030-x
//
// This BioScript file encodes the 10x Chromium 3' Prox-seq
// arm of the protocol (Steps 1-26: probe preparation;
// Steps 27-40: sample processing / PLA ligation;
// Steps 87-102: 10x-based single-cell isolation and library
// construction; Steps 132-147: sequencing, alignment,
// and protein complex quantification).
//
// NOTE ON BIOLOGICAL SCOPE:
// Prox-seq combines a proximity ligation assay (PLA) with
// single-cell mRNA sequencing, enabling simultaneous
// measurement of proteins, mRNA, and hundreds of extracellular
// protein complexes from single cells. Each targeted protein
// is labelled with TWO antibody-DNA probes (probe A and
// probe B). When two probes are within 50-70 nm, a connector
// oligomer bridges them and T4 ligase produces a PLA product
// that is subsequently sequenced. The 10x Chromium 3' V3.1
// workflow captures both mRNA (poly-A capture) and PLA
// products (U_fwd primer) within the same GEM droplet.
//
// NOTE ON PROBE CONJUGATION ABSTRACTION:
// Steps 1-26 involve copper-free click chemistry: antibodies
// are first conjugated to DBCO via NHS ester chemistry, then
// reacted overnight with azide-bearing DNA oligomers. In
// BioScript, `mix` abstracts both the NHS conjugation
// incubation and the click-chemistry overnight reaction.
// `heat` models the on-ice incubation for NHS ester coupling
// (0c / 60 min) and the room-temperature buffer-exchange
// centrifugation cycles are abstracted as `mix` steps.
// The DBCO UV-visible QC check (309 nm absorbance, molar
// extinction coefficient 12,000 M-1 cm-1) and antibody QC
// check (280 nm, 204,000 M-1 cm-1) are both captured by
// the dbcoConjugationQC detection module.
//
// NOTE ON PLA LIGATION ABSTRACTION:
// Steps 27-40: cells are pelleted, washed in 1% BSA/PBS,
// resuspended with Prox-seq probe mixture (2.5 nM each
// probe per target protein), incubated at 37 C for 30-60 min,
// washed three times, and then resuspended in ligation buffer
// (50 mM HEPES pH 7.5, 10 mM MgCl2, 1 mM rATP, 9.5 nM
// connector oligomer, 130 U/mL T4 ligase). A 30 min ligation
// at 37 C produces PLA products from probe pairs within
// 50-70 nm. `mix` abstracts the cell-probe incubation and
// ligation steps; `heat` models 37 C incubations. Two
// post-ligation washes are abstracted as a final `mix`.
//
// NOTE ON 10x CHROMIUM ABSTRACTION:
// Steps 87-102: cells are filtered (40 um strainer), loaded
// onto the Chromium Controller with GEL beads and partitioning
// oil, generating GEMs (~20,000 viable cells input required).
// The U_fwd primer (2 uM final, added to the amplification
// mix at Step 90) co-amplifies PLA products alongside cDNA.
// SPRI size selection at 0.6x (Step 91) separates PLA products
// (supernatant, ~100 bp pre-index) from cDNA (bead-bound,
// ~1,000 bp). Supernatant is saved for PLA library construction
// (CRITICAL: supernatant discarded in standard 10x protocol).
// cDNA is eluted and processed per 10x 3' V3.1 standard.
// PLA products are indexed with 10x_SI_PCR + P7_N70X_Custom2
// primers (12 PCR cycles, 60 C anneal) and size-selected at
// 2.1x SPRI to yield a ~228 bp indexed library (Fig. 2f).
//
// NOTE ON COMPILER CONSTRAINT (lilott8/BioScript):
// Duration tokens: s (seconds) and m (minutes) only.
// Overnight incubations (Step 25: 16 h) -> 960m.
// 30-60 min probe incubation -> 45m (midpoint).
// Multi-unit dispense does not produce discrete array elements;
// all reagents are instantiated as scalar variables.
// `drain` is used for failed QC branches; `dispose` for
// successfully consumed intermediates and QC signal droplets.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- entry: probe preparation,
//                              sample processing, PLA ligation,
//                              10x GEM generation, cDNA & PLA
//                              library construction
//   BB2  dbcoPass           -- dbcoSignal > 0: DBCO conjugation
//                              successful (ratio 1-10 DBCO/Ab);
//                              proceed to oligo conjugation
//   BB3  dbcoFail           -- dbcoSignal <= 0: conjugation
//                              failed or ratio out of range;
//                              drain and abort
//   BB4  dbcoJoin           -- join: oligo conjugation and
//                              probe storage
//   BB5  libraryPass        -- librarySignal > 0: cDNA peak at
//                              ~1,000 bp and PLA peak at ~100 bp
//                              confirmed by TapeStation; proceed
//                              to final library construction
//   BB6  libraryFail        -- librarySignal <= 0: no clear PLA
//                              peak or cDNA yield too low; drain
//   BB7  libraryJoin        -- join: final PLA library indexing
//                              and sequencing preparation
//   BB8  assayPass          -- assaySignal > 0: PLA product
//                              library at ~228 bp confirmed;
//                              proceed to sequencing
//   BB9  assayFail          -- assaySignal <= 0: PLA library QC
//                              failed; drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose all QC signals;
//                              experiment ends
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 1-12: Buffer exchange for each antibody.
//   For each antibody, wet a 50,000 MWCO Amicon Ultra-0.5
//   concentrator with 500 uL PBS; spin at 14,000g / 4 C
//   (1 min, 5 min, 5 min, 10 min cycles). Three consecutive
//   PBS washes exchange the antibody storage buffer (which
//   may contain BSA or gelatin -- CRITICAL: incompatible with
//   DBCO NHS ester) into clean PBS.
//   `mix` abstracts the concentrator wash/spin cycles.
//   Representative single antibody shown; panel of antibodies
//   (Supplementary Table 1) would be parallelised off-chip.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rawAntibody      = dispense 1 units of PBS
antibodyPBS      = dispense 1 units of PBS

// First buffer-exchange wash cycle (Steps 4-7: 500 uL PBS, 5 min spin)
bufferExchange1  = mix rawAntibody with antibodyPBS for 5m

// Second buffer-exchange wash cycle (Steps 8-10: 450 uL PBS, 5 min spin)
antibodyPBS2     = dispense 1 units of PBS
bufferExchange2  = mix bufferExchange1 with antibodyPBS2 for 5m

// Third buffer-exchange wash cycle (Steps 11-12: 450 uL PBS, 10 min spin)
antibodyPBS3     = dispense 1 units of PBS
concentratedAb   = mix bufferExchange2 with antibodyPBS3 for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 13-17: Prepare 2 mM DBCO stock solution.
//   Dissolve dibenzocyclooctyne-PEG4-N-hydroxysuccinimidyl
//   ester (Sigma-Aldrich 764019) in 10 uL DMSO; take 1 uL
//   aliquot, dilute 100x in PBS, measure absorbance at 309 nm
//   on Nanodrop (molar extinction coefficient 12,000 M-1 cm-1).
//   Prepare to 2 mM final in DMSO.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dmsoSolvent      = dispense 1 units of DMSO
dbcoNHS          = dispense 1 units of DBCO_NHS_Ester
dbcoStock        = mix dbcoNHS with dmsoSolvent for 2s

// QC dilution (1 uL into 100 uL PBS) for Nanodrop 309 nm read.
pbsDilutionQC    = dispense 1 units of PBS
dbcoDiluted      = mix dbcoStock with pbsDilutionQC for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 18-19: DBCO conjugation to antibody.
//   Combine 2 mM DBCO (DMSO) with concentrated antibody at
//   1:10 volume ratio (CRITICAL: antibody concentration must
//   be 0.5-2 mg/mL before conjugation). Incubate on ice 1 h.
//   Reaction time can be extended to 2 h without negative effect.
//   `heat` at 0c models the on-ice incubation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dbcoReaction     = mix dbcoDiluted with concentratedAb for 2s
heat dbcoReaction at 0c for 60m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 20-23: Purify DBCO-conjugated antibody and QC.
//   Repeat concentrator wash (Steps 4-12) to remove unconjugated
//   DBCO. Measure absorbances at 280 nm (antibody) and 309 nm
//   (DBCO) on Nanodrop. Calculate DBCO:antibody molar ratio
//   (target: 1-10 DBCO per antibody; reactions most reliable
//   at 100 ug input). Store aliquots at -20 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

purifyPBS1       = dispense 1 units of PBS
purifiedDbcoAb1  = mix dbcoReaction with purifyPBS1 for 5m

purifyPBS2       = dispense 1 units of PBS
purifiedDbcoAb2  = mix purifiedDbcoAb1 with purifyPBS2 for 5m

purifyPBS3       = dispense 1 units of PBS
purifiedDbcoAb   = mix purifiedDbcoAb2 with purifyPBS3 for 10m

// DBCO conjugation QC: detect absorbance at 280 nm and 309 nm.
// Module checks that DBCO:Ab ratio is within 1-10 range (Fig. 2b).
dbcoSignal       = detect dbcoConjugationQC on purifiedDbcoAb for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: DBCO conjugation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): dbcoSignal > 0 -> DBCO:Ab ratio acceptable;
//             proceed to oligo conjugation (Step 24).
// Fail (BB3): dbcoSignal <= 0 -> conjugation failed (low input
//             mass, excessive DBCO ratio, or buffer interference);
//             drain and abort probe preparation.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (dbcoJoin).
// ============================================================

if (dbcoSignal > 0) {
    dispose dbcoReaction
} else {
    drain dbcoReaction
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: dbcoJoin
// Dispose DBCO QC signal. Control falls into oligo conjugation
// and probe assembly (Steps 24-26).
// ============================================================

dispose dbcoSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 24-26: Conjugate azide-DNA oligomers to DBCO-antibody.
//   Combine 2 ug DBCO-conjugated antibody with equal volume of
//   80 uM azide-functionalized oligonucleotides (IDT custom;
//   Probe A and Probe B oligos have unique DNA barcodes;
//   sequences from Vistain et al. Nat. Methods 2022).
//   Incubate overnight at 4 C (copper-free click chemistry;
//   DBCO reacts with azide without Cu catalyst).
//   Reaction can be extended to 2 d without negative effect.
//   Overnight (16 h) = 960 min.
//   Store finished probes in 50% (wt/vol) glycerol/PBS at -20 C;
//   stable for >=1 year.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oligoA           = dispense 1 units of AzideDNA_OligoA
oligoB           = dispense 1 units of AzideDNA_OligoB

// Combine probe A oligo with DBCO-antibody
probeA_raw       = mix purifiedDbcoAb with oligoA for 2s

// Combine probe B oligo with a second DBCO-antibody aliquot
// (each target protein requires one probe A and one probe B)
purifiedDbcoAb_B = dispense 1 units of PBS
probeB_raw       = mix purifiedDbcoAb_B with oligoB for 2s

// Overnight click-chemistry incubation at 4 C (960 min = 16 h).
heat probeA_raw at 4c for 960m
heat probeB_raw at 4c for 960m

// Probe panel assembled: both probe A and probe B are ready.
// Pool probes in probe binding buffer (PBS + 0.1% BSA +
// 0.1 mg/mL sonicated salmon sperm DNA + 6.7 nM per isotype).
salmonSpermDNA   = dispense 1 units of SalmonSpermDNA
bsaPBS           = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS

probeBindingBuf  = mix salmonSpermDNA with bsaPBS for 2s
probeA           = mix probeA_raw with probeBindingBuf for 2s

probeBindingBuf2 = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS
probeB           = mix probeB_raw with probeBindingBuf2 for 2s

// Final probe panel: 2.5 nM probe A + 2.5 nM probe B per target
// (5 nM total per targeted protein).
proxseqProbePanel = mix probeA with probeB for 2s

// ============================================================
// STEPS 27-40: Sample Processing (PLA ligation)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 27-31: Cell pelleting and initial wash.
//   Centrifuge cells at 300-500g / 4 C / 5 min.
//   Resuspend in 1 mL 1% (wt/vol) BSA/PBS.
//   Repeat spin and discard supernatant.
//   `mix` abstracts the resuspension step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

singleCellSample  = dispense 1 units of SingleCells
fcxBlocker        = dispense 1 units of TruStain_FcX
bsaWash           = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS

// Fc receptor blocking (TruStain FcX) prevents non-specific
// antibody binding; add before probe staining.
blockedCells      = mix singleCellSample with fcxBlocker for 10m

// First BSA/PBS wash
washedCells1      = mix blockedCells with bsaWash for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 32-34: Probe staining.
//   Resuspend cell pellet in Prox-seq probe mixture at 2.5 nM
//   per probe (30 uL per 100,000 cells). Incubate at 37 C for
//   30-60 min (45 min modelled here as midpoint).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

stainedCells      = mix washedCells1 with proxseqProbePanel for 45m
heat stainedCells at 37c for 45m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 35: Three post-staining washes.
//   Wash three times with 1 mL 1% (wt/vol) BSA/PBS by
//   centrifugation. If overprocessing is a concern, reduce
//   washes by at least one.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaWash2          = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS
bsaWash3          = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS
bsaWash4          = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS

wash1             = mix stainedCells with bsaWash2 for 2m
wash2             = mix wash1 with bsaWash3 for 2m
wash3             = mix wash2 with bsaWash4 for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 36-37: PLA ligation.
//   Resuspend washed cell pellet in 100 uL ligation buffer
//   (50 mM HEPES pH 7.5, 10 mM MgCl2, 1 mM rATP, 9.5 nM
//   connector oligomer TTTCACGACACGACACGATTTAGGTC,
//   130 U/mL T4 ligase). Incubate at 37 C for 30 min.
//   When two probes on the same cell surface are within
//   50-70 nm, the connector bridges them and T4 ligase
//   joins the two oligos to form a PLA ligation product.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ligBuffer         = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
t4Ligase          = dispense 1 units of T4_Ligase
rnaseInhib        = dispense 1 units of RNaseInhibitor

ligationMix       = mix ligBuffer with t4Ligase for 2s
ligationMixFull   = mix ligationMix with rnaseInhib for 2s
ligatedCells      = mix wash3 with ligationMixFull for 2s
heat ligatedCells at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 39: Two post-ligation washes.
//   Remove excess connector oligo and ligase before 10x loading.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bsaWash5          = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS
bsaWash6          = dispense 1 units of BlockerBSA_PBS

postLigWash1      = mix ligatedCells with bsaWash5 for 2m
postLigWash2      = mix postLigWash1 with bsaWash6 for 2m

// FIX #1 (v3): Decouple viableCells from stainedForSort entirely.
//
// Root cause of viableCells2[0] dangling ref:
// The compiler uses strict SSA single-use token semantics. When
// viableCells was derived from stainedForSort (which was already
// consumed by detect), the compiler incremented the SSA slot on
// the second downstream use in bsbbif_7_j -> viableCells2[0],
// which was never assigned.
//
// Fix: both viableCells and stainedForSort now derive INDEPENDENTLY
// from postLigWash2. Each gets its own separate dispense of the
// relevant reagent and its own mix lineage. Neither variable
// appears in the other's def-use chain, so the compiler assigns
// each a unique [0] slot with no aliasing or increment.
//
// Protocol fidelity: this correctly models the paper's intent --
// Step 39 washes yield a clean cell pellet (postLigWash2); dead
// cell removal (Miltenyi kit) and PI viability staining are
// parallel QC operations on that same pellet, not sequential.

deadCellKit       = dispense 1 units of DeadCellRemovalKit
piStain           = dispense 1 units of PropidiumIodide

// Dead cell removal path: postLigWash2 -> Miltenyi kit -> viableCells
// viableCells is the input to the 10x Chromium Controller (Step 87).
viableCells       = mix postLigWash2 with deadCellKit for 10m

// Viability QC path: postLigWash2 -> PI stain -> detect -> gate
// stainedForSort is consumed by detect; viableCells is independent.
stainedForSort    = mix postLigWash2 with piStain for 5m
viabilitySignal   = detect viabilityDetection on stainedForSort for 30s

// FIX #1 (v4): viableCells must NOT appear inside either branch.
// Compiler liveness rule: any variable consumed (dispose or drain)
// inside a branch is marked dead at the subsequent join block.
// If viableCells is drained in the fail branch, the compiler sees it
// as dead entering bsbbif_7_j and allocates viableCells2[0] for the
// downstream use there -- a dangling ref never assigned.
// Solution: leave viableCells completely untouched in BOTH branches.
// Only stainedForSort (the QC-only variable) is disposed/drained.
// viableCells flows through the gate unconsumed and is picked up
// cleanly as viableCells1[0] in bsbbif_7_j by the Chromium GEM step.
if (viabilitySignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedForSort
} else {
    drain stainedForSort
}

dispose viabilitySignal

// ============================================================
// STEPS 87-102: 10x Chromium 3'-based Prox-seq
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 87-89: Dead cell removal and cell filtration.
//   Filter cells through 40 um cell strainer to remove clumps.
//   Load 20,000 viable cells onto 10x Chromium Controller with
//   Chromium Next GEM Chip G and GEL beads (3' v3.1 kit,
//   cat. 1000268). Generate GEMs per 10x manufacturer protocol
//   until just before cDNA amplification.
//   `mix` abstracts the microfluidic GEM partitioning step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

chromiumGELBeads  = dispense 1 units of Chromium_GELBeads
chromiumOil       = dispense 1 units of Chromium_Oil

// GEM generation: cells + GEL beads + partitioning oil
// Chromium Controller encapsulates single cells in GEMs.
gemDroplets       = mix viableCells with chromiumGELBeads for 2s
gemEmulsion       = mix gemDroplets with chromiumOil for 45m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 90: cDNA amplification with U_fwd primer addition.
//   CRITICAL: add 1 uL of 2 uM U_fwd primer to the
//   amplification mix along with standard 10x cDNA primers.
//   U_fwd primer co-amplifies PLA ligation products alongside
//   cDNA. Run 12 PCR cycles per 10x Genomics instructions.
//   Without U_fwd, PLA products are lost in the standard
//   10x protocol.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

kapaReadyMix      = dispense 1 units of KAPA_HiFi_ReadyMix
dntpMix           = dispense 1 units of dNTP_Mix

ampMix            = mix kapaReadyMix with dntpMix for 2s
amplifiedProduct  = mix gemEmulsion with ampMix for 2s

// 12-cycle PCR amplification per 10x Genomics 3' V3.1 protocol.
// Denature: 98 C; anneal: 60-67 C; extend: 72 C.
// Modelled as a heat step representing total PCR duration (~30 min).
heat amplifiedProduct at 72c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 91-93: SPRI size selection to separate PLA from cDNA.
//   Add 60 uL SPRIselect beads to amplified product at 0.6x
//   final volume ratio; incubate 5 min at room temperature.
//   CRITICAL: save 75 uL supernatant -- this contains the
//   PLA products (~100 bp). In the standard 10x protocol
//   this supernatant is DISCARDED; in Prox-seq it is retained.
//   cDNA fragments (~1,000 bp) remain on SPRIselect beads.
//   Wash beads 2x with 80% ethanol; elute cDNA into 35 uL
//   Buffer EB.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// FIX #2 (v3): Split the 0.6x SPRI step into two fully independent
// dispensation lineages -- one for cDNA, one for PLA.
//
// Root cause of spriMix12[0] dangling ref:
// spriMix1 was consumed twice: once by elutedCDNA (cDNA elution)
// and once by plaCleanup (PLA supernatant cleanup). BioScript's
// SSA single-use token semantics allocated spriMix12[0] on the
// second use, which was never assigned.
//
// Fix: dispense two independent sets of SPRI beads and produce
// two independent mix variables -- spriMix_cDNA and spriMix_PLA --
// both derived from amplifiedProduct. Each is consumed exactly once
// downstream. The compiler assigns each a [0] slot with no
// increment or aliasing.
//
// Protocol fidelity: this correctly models Step 91-93 of the paper.
// The physical 0.6x SPRI step separates one pool of amplified GEM
// product into a bead-bound cDNA fraction and a free PLA supernatant.
// BioScript cannot model a physical split from a single variable,
// so two parallel mix operations on the same upstream variable
// (amplifiedProduct) faithfully represent the two output fractions.

spriBeads_cDNA    = dispense 1 units of SPRIselect_Beads
spriBeads_PLA     = dispense 1 units of SPRIselect_Beads

// cDNA path: amplifiedProduct + beads -> bead-bound cDNA fraction.
// cDNA (~1,000 bp) binds SPRIselect beads at 0.6x ratio.
spriMix_cDNA      = mix amplifiedProduct with spriBeads_cDNA for 5m

// PLA path: amplifiedProduct + beads -> free supernatant PLA fraction.
// PLA products (~100 bp) do not bind at 0.6x and remain in supernatant.
// CRITICAL (Step 92): in standard 10x protocol this supernatant is
// discarded; in Prox-seq it is retained for PLA library construction.
spriMix_PLA       = mix amplifiedProduct with spriBeads_PLA for 5m

// TapeStation QC: cDNA peak at ~1,000 bp (Fig. 2c).
// PLA peak in supernatant at ~100 bp (Fig. 2d).
bufferEB1         = dispense 1 units of BufferEB
elutedCDNA        = mix spriMix_cDNA with bufferEB1 for 5m

librarySignal     = detect proxseqLibraryQC on elutedCDNA for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Pre-amplification library QC gate
// Pass (BB5): librarySignal > 0 -> cDNA at ~1,000 bp and PLA
//             at ~100 bp confirmed by TapeStation; proceed to
//             final library construction (Steps 95-102).
// Fail (BB6): librarySignal <= 0 -> no clear PLA peak or cDNA
//             yield too low (check AMPure bead volume, avoid
//             over-drying); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (libraryJoin).
// ============================================================

// FIX #2 (v4): spriMix_PLA must NOT appear inside either branch.
// Same compiler liveness rule as Fix #1: spriMix_PLA is consumed in
// both BB8_t and BB9_f branches -> compiler marks it dead at bsbbif_10_j
// -> allocates spriMix_PLA2[0] for the plaCleanup use -> dangling ref.
// Solution: only dispose/drain spriMix_cDNA inside the gate (it has no
// downstream use after elutedCDNA). spriMix_PLA flows through both
// branches untouched and remains live as spriMix_PLA1[0] in bsbbif_10_j
// where it is consumed by mix(spriMix_PLA, spriBeads2) for plaCleanup.
if (librarySignal > 0) {
    dispose spriMix_cDNA
} else {
    drain spriMix_cDNA
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: libraryJoin
// Dispose pre-amplification library QC signal. Control falls
// into final library construction (Steps 95-102).
// ============================================================

dispose librarySignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 95: Gene expression library construction (cDNA).
//   Use 10 uL of purified cDNA product as input to standard
//   10x Genomics single-cell 3' V3.1 gene expression library
//   protocol. Number of PCR cycles determined by cDNA input.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tenxLibraryKit    = dispense 1 units of KAPA_HiFi_ReadyMix
gexLibrary        = mix elutedCDNA with tenxLibraryKit for 30m
heat gexLibrary at 72c for 20m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEPS 96-102: PLA product library construction.
//   Clean up PLA supernatant with 70 uL SPRIselect beads at
//   2.1x final volume ratio. Wash 2x 80% ethanol; elute into
//   40 uL Buffer EB.
//   Verify PLA products by TapeStation (peak at ~100 bp; Fig. 2d).
//   PCR reaction (50 uL total): 10 uL PLA product + KAPA HiFi
//   HotStart Readymix + 0.2 uM 10x_SI_PCR primer +
//   0.2 uM P7_N70X_Custom2 primer + nuclease-free water.
//   PCR program: 98 C 2 min; then 12 cycles (98 C 20s /
//   60 C 30s / 72 C 20s); 72 C 5 min; hold 4 C.
//   Clean up with 60 uL SPRIselect beads at 1.2x; elute into
//   40 uL Buffer EB. Final PLA library: ~228 bp (Fig. 2f).
//   Store at -20 C until sequencing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 2.1x SPRI cleanup of PLA supernatant (spriMix_PLA, ~100 bp fraction).
// spriMix_PLA is consumed exactly once here; no SSA slot increment.
spriBeads2        = dispense 1 units of SPRIselect_Beads
bufferEB2         = dispense 1 units of BufferEB

plaCleanup        = mix spriMix_PLA with spriBeads2 for 5m
plaEluted         = mix plaCleanup with bufferEB2 for 5m

kapaForPLA        = dispense 1 units of KAPA_HiFi_ReadyMix
nfWater           = dispense 1 units of NucleaseFreeWater

plaPcrMix         = mix kapaForPLA with nfWater for 2s
plaAmplified      = mix plaEluted with plaPcrMix for 2s

// 12-cycle PCR: index PLA products with 10x_SI_PCR + P7_N70X_Custom2.
// Anneal at 60 C (lower than cDNA library due to short amplicon).
heat plaAmplified at 60c for 25m

// Final 1.2x SPRI cleanup of indexed PLA library.
spriBeads3        = dispense 1 units of SPRIselect_Beads
bufferEB3         = dispense 1 units of BufferEB

plaSpriClean      = mix plaAmplified with spriBeads3 for 5m
plaLibrary        = mix plaSpriClean with bufferEB3 for 5m

// Final QC: Qubit fluorometer (concentration) + Agilent high-
// sensitivity TapeStation (size distribution; target ~228 bp).
assaySignal       = detect plaProductDetection on plaLibrary for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Final PLA library QC gate
// Pass (BB8): assaySignal > 0 -> PLA library peak confirmed
//             at ~228 bp by TapeStation (Fig. 2f); yield
//             confirmed by Qubit; proceed to sequencing.
// Fail (BB9): assaySignal <= 0 -> no clear 228 bp peak
//             (check AMPure bead volume, avoid carryover beads,
//             check for adapter dimers <200 bp); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (assaySignal > 0) {
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEPS 133, 132-134: Next-generation sequencing on
    //   NextSeq 500/550.
    //   10x-based Prox-seq: sequence cDNA and PLA libraries
    //   SEPARATELY (pooling at 4:1 mRNA:PLA recommended for
    //   Drop-seq; 10x libraries are sequenced on separate runs).
    //
    //   cDNA library: high-output 150-cycle kit.
    //     Read 1: 28 cycles; i7 index: 10 cycles;
    //     i5 index: 10 cycles; Read 2: 90 cycles.
    //     1% vol/vol PhiX spike-in.
    //
    //   PLA library: mid-output 150-cycle kit.
    //     Read 1: 28 cycles; i7 index: 8 cycles;
    //     Read 2: 75 cycles.
    //     40% vol/vol PhiX spike-in (CRITICAL: high PhiX
    //     required due to low PLA library complexity).
    //     Spike in custom read 2 primer (DropPLA_Read2) to
    //     Illumina read 2 primer; prepare custom i7 read primer
    //     (DropPLA_i7Read) per Illumina instructions.
    //
    //   `mix` abstracts library pooling + PhiX spike-in prep.
    //   `heat` models the cluster generation / sequencing run
    //   duration (~8-10 h for mid-output NextSeq 550 run).
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    phiXControl       = dispense 1 units of PhiX_Control
    seqKit            = dispense 1 units of NextSeq_MidOutput_Kit

    // Pool GEX library + PhiX (1% spike-in for cDNA run)
    gexSeqPool        = mix gexLibrary with phiXControl for 5m

    // Pool PLA library + PhiX (40% spike-in for PLA run)
    phiXForPLA        = dispense 1 units of PhiX_Control
    plaSeqPool        = mix plaLibrary with phiXForPLA for 5m

    seqRunMix         = mix plaSeqPool with seqKit for 2s

    // NextSeq 550 sequencing run: ~8-10 h for mid-output kit.
    // Modelled as 600 min heat step at 4c (instrument temperature).
    heat seqRunMix at 4c for 600m

    dispose gexSeqPool
    dispose seqRunMix

} else {
    drain plaLibrary
    drain gexLibrary
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose the PLA library QC signal droplet.
// Experiment ends. Downstream steps (alignment, protein
// complex quantification) are computational:
//
// STEPS 135-138 (cDNA alignment):
//   BCL -> FASTQ (BCL Convert). Align with Cell Ranger v6.1.1+:
//   `cellranger mkref` (reference genome index) then
//   `cellranger count` (alignment + cell-barcode matrix).
//
// STEPS 139-143 (PLA alignment):
//   Custom Java program (PLA_alignment.jar; github.com/tay-lab/
//   Prox-seq). Commands: ReadAlignment10x (extract cell barcode
//   + UMI + probe identities from FASTQ); BulidCellBarcodes
//   (cell reference list); CellBarcodeCorrection; UMIMerging
//   (merge PLA products from same cell with similar UMIs);
//   DigitalCount (export DPE matrix as text file).
//
// STEPS 144-145 (protein abundance):
//   Python script (github.com/tay-lab/NProt_data-src).
//   Import DPE matrix -> PLA object; call
//   `calculateProteinCount` -> `protein_count` dataframe.
//
// STEPS 146-147 (protein complex quantification):
//   Call `predictComplex` method (default: 'iterative' method;
//   alternative: 'lr' weighted least-squares regression,
//   compatible with free-oligo variant only) ->
//   `complex_count` dataframe.
//   Apply double filtering: mRNA-based cell barcode correction +
//   filter cells with too few or too many PLA product UMIs.
//   Integrate mRNA + protein + protein complex count matrices
//   for multimodal single-cell analysis (Seurat / Scanpy).
// ============================================================

dispose assaySignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
